The inheritance structure `struct Derived : public Base` is specific to C++ (not C) and is not valid for a C program, as was the intention of the lab. Instead, you would embed the base class at the top of the class. Something like:

```c
struct Plane {
    struct Vehicle base;
    ...
```

Honestly, everything else looks good, the only thing I could think of is to consider spacing the printf statement out over multiple lines like: 
printf("Plane start. Speed: %.1f, Altitude: %d\n",
          self->base.speed,
          self->altitude
);
which I think would make it a little more readable.

